          "date": "2026-11-25 17:49:52.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21337 utils: keep the last character of netlink stats lines",
        "message": "LU-21337 utils: keep the last character of netlink stats lines\n\nA user who is not root reads stats over Netlink.  The plain output of\n\"lctl get_param <obd>.*.stats\" lost the last character of each counter\nline, so the last field (sum of squares) was wrong, and a one-digit\nvalue printed as an empty field.  Root (debugfs) and -y were correct.\n\nprint_out_stats() puts a space before each field, then cut the last\ncharacter to \"eat last white space\", but there was no trailing space.\nRemove the cut.\n\nAdd sanity test_104f, which compares the non-root llite stats lines\nwith the debugfs lines for counters that did not change between the\ntwo reads.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTLC-bug-id: TLU-367\nSigned-off-by: Minh Diep <mdiep@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5\nChange-Id: I62f38af21a7f0ed891c441a85d4deb2bf2cd337e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
